<!-- ===== FAQ ===== -->
<section class="section" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header fade-in">
      <span class="section-tag">Common Questions</span>
      <h2 id="graduate-faq">Honest answers about membership.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mem-faq-wrap fade-in">

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is the free Protégé tier really free?</summary>
        <p>Yes. No card, no trial, no expiration. The full base app is yours forever. Insider and above are paid upgrades. There is nothing hidden.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What's included in Insider that's not in Protégé?</summary>
        <p>Live group sessions with Dr. TJ, deeper education content (Months 5+, advanced protocols), member-only pricing on Rx, supplements, and environmental products, and access to the private Insider community. Protégé gives you the framework — Insider is where the work compounds.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>When does Insider open?</summary>
        <p>Insider pricing is finalizing. Use the "Notify me" buttons on this page to subscribe — we will honor the early-member rate for everyone on the list when we launch. You won't need to do anything except show up.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can I downgrade from Concierge to Insider?</summary>
        <p>Yes, anytime. Downgrading adjusts your access tier at the start of the next billing cycle. You keep your Insider-level access until that date. There are no penalties and no locked-in commitments on paid tiers.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What if I miss a live session?</summary>
        <p>Recordings are available to all active Insider-tier members — Insider, Plus, and Concierge. You will not lose access to session content if life gets in the way of attending live.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Does the member pricing apply to environmental products too?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Member pricing covers Rx, supplements, and environmental products — air quality, water filtration, light optimization, EMF mitigation. The same tier-based discount (10% Insider / 15% Plus / 20% Concierge) applies across the board.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How do I become a Graduate?</summary>
        <p id="graduate-faq-how">12+ months of continuous Insider participation plus completion of specific 4M program milestones (criteria are being formalized as the cohort matures). Graduates earn permanent member benefits including future sharing-program access. Graduate status is earned — it cannot be purchased, and it is the only status in this program that works that way.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How does Graduate status differ from Concierge?</summary>
        <p>Concierge is a paid subscription you can start or stop at any time. Graduate is a permanent earned designation — once you earn it, it doesn't expire and you don't pay a recurring fee to keep it. The tradeoffs are intentional: Concierge gives you the most direct weekly access to Dr. TJ while you are actively paying; Graduate gives you lifetime product pricing and Phase 2 access as a permanent reward for the work you put in.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What's the My4MLife sharing program?</summary>
        <p>A future Phase 2 vehicle for Graduates: a wellness-focused mutual-aid sharing program designed to cover what insurance won't — peptides, longevity protocols, off-label Rx, and environmental products. It is sequestered for now. Graduates will be the first to access it when it launches.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can I cancel a paid tier?</summary>
        <p>Yes, for any paid tier at any time. Protégé does not require a subscription — the app is simply yours. Cancellation of a paid tier returns you to Protégé access at your next billing date.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Why is membership structured this way?</summary>
        <p>Because the work compounds. Day 1 you don't need 1:1 attention — you need the framework. Six months in, you have earned more direct support. A year in, you have earned Graduate-level pricing for life. The structure mirrors the reality of the protocol. Selling you more than you can use at the beginning would just be extractive.</p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is this a medical program?</summary>
        <p>My4MLife provides health education, protocol design, and AI-driven coaching. Medical care, diagnosis, and prescriptions — where required — are provided by contracted licensed telemedicine professionals. Dr. Mundheim is a Doctor of Chiropractic and does not provide medical care through this platform.</p>
      </details>

    </div>
